        {
          "text": "**The vendor is Litware Logistics (V-LITWARE), and no, we can't pay them right now.** Their vendor record is marked **blocked**, and our rules don't allow payments to blocked vendors, so I didn't propose one.\n\n**Invoice INV-106:**\n- **Amount:** 4,000.00 USDC\n- **Due:** 2026-11-18\n- **Invoice status:** Open\n- **Vendor's note:** \"Freight charges for October.\" It's just a description and doesn't ask for anything unusual, like a different address or urgent payment.\n- **Existing payments:** None proposed or made yet.\n- **Registered payout address:** 0x14943d1f674947f9336109c920CD10daB96BCfDd\n\n**What you need to do:** The block on the vendor record has to be resolved before this can be paid. If the block was intended, for example because of a compliance or fraud hold, the invoice should probably stay unpaid or be marked disputed. If it was a mistake, whoever manages vendor records will need to unblock Litware. After that, I can propose the payment for review.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
